{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 capacity, 90.2% initial efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with 13.1% thickness expansion after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalable production and enhanced cycling stability for practical lithium-ion batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The material reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 80% capacity retention in 1200 cycles for pouch cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore engineering as a scalable strategy for developing mechanically stable silicon-carbon anodes with minimal expansion, advancing practical high-energy lithium-ion battery technology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ brain cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 mark distinct repression modes. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated single-cell epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states defined by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal epigenomic atlas provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing the biodegradation of compostable polyesters in deep-sea environments by embedding enzymes within them. The researchers tested thermally embedded enzymes in PBS, PBSA, PCL, and PBAT polyesters, demonstrating accelerated degradation at depths up to 5,503 meters. Enzyme-embedded polyesters achieved near-complete degradation at 757 meters within five months and showed moderate biodegradation at extreme depths. The approach maintains mechanical properties while enabling efficient marine breakdown, offering a potential solution for marine plastic pollution.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Enzyme-embedded polyesters degraded near-completely at 757 m depth within 5 months",
    "Moderate biodegradation observed at extreme deep-sea depths (5,503 m)",
    "Mechanical properties of enzyme-embedded polyesters matched enzyme-free counterparts"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy provides a scalable method for accelerating marine biodegradation of compostable plastics, addressing a critical gap in deep-sea plastic breakdown."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors in ILC3s, promoting inflammation",
    "PRKAR1A deletion reduces ILC3 numbers and increases enteric infection susceptibility",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreases PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used scanning tunneling microscopy to investigate quantum melting transitions in generalized Wigner crystals (GWCs) and Mott insulators within twisted molybdenum diselenide bilayers. It revealed electron-hole asymmetry during GWC melting: electron-doped systems formed delocalized liquid-like states, while hole-doped systems exhibited interaction-driven disorder. The asymmetry stems from broken particle-hole symmetry in the moiré superlattice, creating distinct electron and hole Fermi pockets with different momentum geometries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Electron-doped GWCs melted into delocalized liquid-like states",
    "Hole-doped GWCs formed interaction-driven disordered states",
    "Broken particle-hole symmetry in the moiré superlattice generated distinct electron and hole Fermi pockets with different momentum geometries"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides direct visualization of emergent phases during quantum melting transitions in generalized Wigner crystals, revealing electron-hole asymmetry as a consequence of broken particle-hole symmetry in moiré superlattices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and create a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved 24.84% power conversion efficiency in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, worsening moisture ingress",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how drought and disease alter predator interactions among top vertebrates. Using field observations, researchers found that a decline in shared prey (rabbits) due to disease triggered lynx to prey on kites exclusively during droughts. This behavior reduced kite reproductive success and caused dispersal, while increasing small owl populations. The findings highlight diet flexibility and mobility as critical resilience factors under climatic stress.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Drought and disease caused lynx to prey on k. kites after rabbit decline",
    "Lynx predation reduced kite reproductive success and induced dispersal",
    "Increased small owl abundance followed raptor population decline"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that climatic stressors can reconfigure predator interactions, revealing diet flexibility and mobility as key resilience mechanisms for apex predators under multiple environmental shocks."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the crystalline structure of Earth's inner core using X-ray experiments. The research identified cubic crystals that may challenge existing models of the inner core's composition. The findings suggest that iron in the Earth's core might exist in a more complex form than previously assumed, potentially influencing geophysical understanding.",
  "key_findings": [
    "X-ray experiments detected cubic crystals in Earth's inner core",
    "These crystals could complicate current models of inner core composition",
    "Iron in Earth's core may exist in a more complex crystalline structure than previously thought"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery of cubic crystals in Earth's inner core provides new insights into the physical state of Earth's core, potentially refining models of planetary formation and geodynamo processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates amorphization of organic small molecule 2,3,7,8-tetraamino-5,10-dihydrophenazine-1,4,6,9-tetraone (TDT) to enhance active site exposure in aqueous ammonium-ion batteries. By disrupting π-π stacking, amorphous TDT achieves high surface area (738 m² g⁻¹), high capacity (242.8 mAh g⁻¹), and exceptional cycling stability (87.1% retention after 817 cycles). The mechanism involves NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage, enabling a full cell with 100% capacity retention over 100,000 cycles at 5 A g⁻¹ and practical Ah-level pouch cell performance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amorphous TDT achieves 738 m² g⁻¹ surface area and 242.8 mAh g⁻¹ capacity at 0.1 A g⁻¹",
    "Amorphous TDT retains 87.1% capacity after 817 cycles (2900 h) and 100% capacity retention over 100,000 cycles at 5 A g⁻¹",
    "NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage mechanisms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "Amorphization of organic small molecules enables high-capacity, long-cycle aqueous ammonium-ion batteries with practical energy density, addressing the critical challenge of active site exposure in molecular stacking."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using natural language to programmatically design functional proteins. Pinal, a 16-billion-parameter foundation model trained on 1.7 billion protein-text pairs, translates functional descriptions into candidate protein sequences and structures. Computational evaluations showed high foldability, functional alignment, and diversity. Experimentally, Pinal designed four proteins with catalytic activity, including a 1.7-fold increase in product titre for a CO2 fixation pathway H-protein compared to native variants.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Pinal designs functional proteins directly from natural-language descriptions without manual constraint reformulation",
    "Generated candidates demonstrated high predicted foldability and functional alignment in computational tests",
    "Experimentally validated catalytic activity for four designed proteins, including a 1.7-fold improvement in a CO2 fixation pathway"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes natural language as a viable high-level interface for programmable protein design, reducing reliance on manual structural or sequence constraints while enabling functional validation without iterative optimization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how the accidental domestication of Clostridium botulinum, a lethal bacterium, was harnessed for medical and cosmetic applications. Researchers traced the historical and biological pathways that transformed this pathogen into the botulinum toxin used in Botox treatments. The findings reveal the unintended evolutionary and practical mechanisms enabling this transition from a deadly pathogen to a widely used therapeutic agent.",
  "key_findings": [
    "C. botulinum was inadvertently domesticated for medical use",
    "The bacterium's transition from a lethal pathogen to a therapeutic agent occurred through historical and biological pathways",
    "Botulinum toxin now serves as a key component in Botox treatments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research elucidates the unexpected evolutionary pathway by which a harmful bacterium became a clinically valuable tool, advancing understanding of pathogen domestication and its applications in medicine."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the relationship between grain boundary amorphicity and ionic transport in antiperovskite solid electrolytes using machine learning interatomic potentials. By varying Cl-/Br- ratios and quantifying inter. amorphicity, the research identifies a volcano-shaped relationship where intermediate halide compositions optimize ionic transport through moderately disordered grain boundaries. The findings demonstrate that controlled anion segregation reduces interfacial resistance, providing a predictive framework for solid-state electrolyte design.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Intermediate Cl-/Br- ratios maximize ionic transport by balancing grain boundary amorphicity",
    "Cl-enriched grain boundaries exhibit excessive order, while Br-enriched regions show excessive disorder",
    "Anion-engineered grain boundaries reduce interfacial resistance through controlled halide segregation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a predictive volcano relationship between structural disorder and ionic transport in antiperovskite solid electrolytes, enabling rational design of low-resistance interfaces through anion engineering."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines challenges in pig-to-human xenotransplantation following successful hyperacute rejection prevention. It identifies immune-mediated graft injuries as a critical bottleneck where conventional diagnostics lack sensitivity for early detection. The study proposes multimodal precision diagnostics to enhance immune surveillance, enabling timely intervention and informing immunosuppressive strategies and organ engineering for improved graft survival.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Recent xenotransplantation advances prevent hyperacute rejection but reveal immune-mediated injuries",
    "Conventional diagnostics fail to detect subclinical graft injury early enough for timely intervention",
    "Multimodal precision diagnostics are proposed to enhance immune surveillance and guide therapeutic strategies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes multimodal precision diagnostics as a critical framework for overcoming immunological barriers in xenotransplantation, advancing the transition from experimental to clinically viable organ transplantation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cosmic inflation signatures and galaxy cluster formation using the Simons Observatory in Chile. The observatory employs microwave telescopes to detect faint signals from the early universe. Results indicate potential evidence for cosmic inflation and galaxy cluster distributions, though the findings require further validation through additional observations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Detection of potential cosmic inflation signatures",
    "Identification of galaxy cluster distributions",
    "Need for additional observations to validate findings"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study advances understanding of the early universe's structure and inflationary physics through microwave observations of cosmic signals."
}

{
  "summary": "This review establishes a state-centered framework for organic mixed ionic-electronic conductors (OMIECs), moving beyond scalar descriptors to model electrochemical operation as multidimensional, history-dependent state trajectories. It introduces a minimal sufficient state basis to distinguish essential coordinates, while waveform history and spatial heterogeneity determine when lumped descriptions remain valid. The framework enables experimental testing of relationships like congruence and kinetic ordering, and recasts electrochromics, OECTs, and energy devices as trajectory selection technologies within a shared electrochemical-state landscape.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A minimal sufficient state basis distinguishes essential from redundant coordinates in OMIECs",
    "Waveform history and spatial heterogeneity define validity of lumped state descriptions",
    "The framework enables experimental testing of congruence, kinetic ordering, and mapping drift"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This framework provides a unified approach to model and design electrochemical trajectories in OMIECs, bridging molecular structure, device architecture, and operational protocols for controllable, reversible, and durable electrochemical functions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a torque-driven molecular machine using a helicene molecule suspended between electrodes. Applying voltage induces unidirectional cyclic rotation with 100% directional preference, reversible by voltage polarity. Current enhancement occurs above a threshold voltage, tunable via molecular stretching or compression. The mechanism explains rotation-induced conductance increases and predicts a transition to continuous rotation at specific voltages.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Voltage-induced unidirectional rotation with 100% directional preference in helicene molecules",
    "Current enhancement above a threshold voltage, tunable by molecular deformation",
    "Rotation explains conductance increases and predicts transition to continuous rotation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a prototype for torque-driven molecular machines with unidirectional rotation and significant current modulation, advancing understanding of current-induced molecular motion and conductance mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the feasibility of deploying a mismatched Ebola vaccine in the Democratic Republic of Congo during the ongoing epidemic. The approach involved initial testing of the vaccine candidate before potential addition of Bundibugyo-specific variants. The research found that the mismatched vaccine could be administered effectively, offering a promising early intervention strategy against the outbreak.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Initial testing of a mismatched Ebola vaccine was feasible in the Democratic Republic of Congo",
    "The vaccine candidate showed potential for early intervention in the ongoing epidemic",
    "Bundibug:go-specific variants may be integrated soon to enhance efficacy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides preliminary evidence that mismatched Ebola vaccines can be rapidly deployed in resource-limited settings, potentially accelerating response to emerging epidemics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates constructing stretchable superhydrophobic perovskite quantum dot (PQD) films with multifunctional properties. Using dual-phase synergistic engineering, replica molding, and femtosecond laser direct writing, the researchers achieved a biomimetic surface and controlled PQD precipitation. The films retained >52% luminescence intensity and >150° water contact angle after 800% tensile deformation, with >90% luminescence retention and >95% recognition accuracy after 240 days of water immersion.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Retained >52% initial luminescence intensity after 800% tensile deformation",
    "Maintained water contact angle >150° under high stretchability",
    "Preserved >90% luminescence intensity and >95% recognition accuracy after 240 days of water exposure"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach demonstrates a dual-phase engineering strategy for creating multifunctional, stable perovskite quantum dot films that maintain optical performance under extreme mechanical and environmental stresses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated ctDNA clearance and clinical outcomes in resectable NSCLC patients from NeoCOAST-2, a phase 2 trial comparing novel perioperative treatments. It measured event-free survival and ctDNA clearance at neoadjuvant Cycle 3 Day 1, finding higher clearance rates with Dato-DXd (72.5%) and a significant correlation between ctDNA clearance and prolonged EFS (HR 0.22).",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dato-DXd achieved the highest ctDNA clearance rate (72.5%) at neoadjuvant Cycle 3 Day 1",
    "ctDNA clearance correlated with improved event-free survival (HR 0.22, 95% CI 0.11-0.45)",
    "Patients with both ctDNA clearance and pathological complete response had significantly better event-free survival (HR 0.10, 95% CI 0.02-0.42)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes ctDNA clearance as a predictive biomarker for improved outcomes in resectable NSCLC, providing a mechanistic basis for integrating liquid biopsies into perioperative risk stratification."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether artificial intelligence could identify overlooked solutions across diverse scientific disciplines. Using 'BootLoops' software, researchers systematically analyzed 22 fields to uncover hidden problem-solving approaches. The approach revealed that AI efficiently locates previously undetected solutions within existing scientific literature, suggesting potential for AI-driven discovery in complex research domains.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AI identified hidden problem-solving approaches in 22 scientific disciplines using BootLoops software",
    "The method efficiently uncovered previously overlooked solutions within existing literature",
    "This approach demonstrates AI's capacity to find solutions that researchers might have missed"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates AI's ability to systematically identify underappreciated solutions across diverse scientific fields, advancing understanding of computational methods for scientific discovery."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with ordered nanostructures. By applying high shear forces during extrusion, the method aligns nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices. The approach enables scalable production of complex 3D architectures with 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid. Post-sintering yields materials with zero volume shrinkage, exceptional thermal stability, and tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) or insulation (0.071 W/m/K) depending on alignment direction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing achieves 55 wt% boron nitride loading in polylactic acid filaments",
    "Aligned nanocomposites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermal stability above polymer melting points",
    "Vertically aligned structures show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) while horizontally aligned ones provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a scalable method for creating nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and long-range ordered nanostructures, enabling precise control over macroscopic properties through nanoscale alignment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a method for depolymerizing silicones into their monomeric form using silylium-ion-initiated chlorination. The approach employs phosgene derivatives as deoxygenative chlorinating agents under mild conditions to cleave Si-O-Si bonds, regenerating dichlorosilane. The process demonstrates broad applicability to various silicone polymers and offers a sustainable recycling pathway for chemically inert sil. The findings enable circular economy integration for silicone waste management.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Silylium-ion-initiated depolymerization cleaves Si-O-Si linkages in siloxanes",
    "Phosgene derivatives act as deoxygenative chlorinating reagents to regenerate dichlorosilane",
    "The method works for diverse linear and cyclic siloxanes including commercial silicone products"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This depolymerization strategy provides a sustainable pathway for recycling chemically inert silicones into high-value monomers, advancing circular economy principles for silicone waste management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether recent global warming has prevented the onset of the next ice age by analyzing a residual continental glacier. The research suggests that current warming trends might have halted the natural progression toward glaciation, indicating a potential shift in Earth's climate cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Analysis of a continental glacier remnant indicates recent global warming may have forestalled the next glaciation",
    "The study implies current climate trends could have interrupted the natural progression toward ice age formation",
    "This finding suggests a possible shift in Earth's long-term climate cycle dynamics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides evidence that contemporary global warming may have altered the trajectory of Earth's natural glacial cycles, offering insights into climate system resilience and the potential for anthropogenic influence on long-term ice age timing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates methods to achieve homogeneous mixed-cation perovskite single crystals for enhanced x-ray detection. Using acetic acid to balance crystallization kinetics of formamidinium and methylammonium phases, the researchers eliminated compositional inhomogeneity. The resulting crystals achieved high sensitivity (3.54 × 1.0e6 µC Gy-1 cm-2), low detection limits (2.65 nGy s-1), and stable performance, demonstrating a kinetic-regulation approach for uniform mixed-cation perovskites.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Acetic acid enables synergistic interaction engineering to balance crystallization rates of formamidinium and methylammonium phases",
    "Elimination of compositional gradients across single crystals through kinetic regulation",
    "X-ray detectors achieved sensitivity of 3.54 × 10^6 µC Gy-1 cm-2 and detection limit of 2.65 nGy s-1"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This kinetic-regulation strategy provides a general method for producing homogeneous mixed-cation perovskite single crystals, advancing x-ray detector performance without compositional inhomogeneity."
}
